---
import Section from '../ui/Section.astro';
import Stack from '../layout/Stack.astro';
import TileRow from '../ui/TileRow.astro';
import Tile from '../ui/Tile.astro';
import ScaleChart from '../ui/ScaleChart.astro';
---

<Section id="budgets" eyebrow="Budgets" title="Budgets, not brags.">
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    Each number below is a limit liam has to stay under. Each one becomes a CI gate, and a commit that misses a budget
    fails the build. When a gate starts measuring, its number on this page is replaced by the measured one.
  </Fragment>
  <Stack gap="7">
    <TileRow>
      <Tile value="25" unit="ms" label="Cold boot to first byte">
        Firecracker microVM, from VMM start to the first HTTP response.
      </Tile>
      <Tile value="5" unit="ms" label="Exec to listening">
        As a container on an existing host kernel. Your site is mapped, not loaded.
      </Tile>
      <Tile value="6" unit="MB" label="Base container image">
        liam-init plus liamd, statically linked. Your site is added on top.
      </Tile>
      <Tile value="0" label="Dropped connections">
        On config reload, binary upgrade, or a liamd crash. The sockets outlive the server.
      </Tile>
    </TileRow>
    <ScaleChart
      title="Drawn to scale"
      note="0 to 400 ms. A blink takes 100 to 400 ms."
      max={400}
      unit="ms"
      ticks={[0, 100, 200, 300, 400]}
      bars={[
        { label: 'liam, container', range: '0 to 5 ms', from: 0, to: 5 },
        { label: 'liam, microVM', range: '0 to 25 ms', from: 0, to: 25 },
        { label: 'One human blink', range: '100 to 400 ms', from: 100, to: 400, tone: 'mark' },
      ]}
    />
  </Stack>
</Section>
